From 1ae2f0c927bf9b1234be9ea2d38b829aa2ca3c1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yeison Delgado <yeisonestivendelgado109@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:34:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(nodes): transformer-layer state per node (US7, F-19 to
 F-23)

GET /nodes now sends transformer_state: CRITICAL with two or more SMAC
phases down, WARNING with exactly one, INACTIVE with none down and the SMAC
inactive, NORMAL otherwise, and null without a transformer. A phase is down
when its last 05xx21y event is a SET. Phases are counted against the
transformer's own phase count from its identifier, so a two-phase
transformer with both phases down is red. A node with several transformers
takes the most severe state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012Za94ATKRpuhbxLyQmG5TG
